USAGE
  {{command}} outbox [list] [--color <when>]
  {{command}} outbox show <id> [--color <when>]
  {{command}} outbox new <unit|message> <markdown> [--send [--yes]]
  {{command}} outbox new <unit|message> --react <emoji> [--send [--yes]]
  {{command}} outbox approve <id> [--text <markdown>] [--yes]
  {{command}} outbox retry <id> [--confirm] [--yes]
  {{command}} outbox edit <id> <markdown>
  {{command}} outbox discard <id> [--reason <why>]

List the drafts waiting on you, proposed, failed or left sending, grouped by
kind, or print one whole: its text as it reads, the items it is about and the
commands it takes. Piped, the list is one tab-separated line per draft: id,
kind, state, unit, label, mentions, creation time and first line. new writes a
reply, or a reaction, on a unit: a Slack message ref (<conversation>/<ts>) or
permalink (its thread, or with --react the message itself), a pull request URL
or owner/repo#n, or <provider>:<key>. It waits in the Outbox for your approval;
with --send it posts once you read it and say yes. approve shows a draft whole
and posts it once you say yes, only from a terminal of your own, never an
agent's shell; retry posts a failed one again. edit changes a draft's text and
discard drops it.

FLAGS
  --color <when>     list, show: auto, always or never
  --react <emoji>    new: react instead of replying: to the Slack message named,
                     else to the unit's message
  --send             new: post it now, through the Outbox, instead of saving it
                     there
  --text <markdown>  approve: post this text instead of the draft's
  --confirm          retry: post again a draft that may have been posted
  --yes              new --send, approve, retry: go ahead without asking
  --reason <why>     discard: why the draft is dropped

EXAMPLES
  {{command}} outbox
  {{command}} outbox new https://acme.slack.com/archives/C0123/p1700000000000100 "Friday works"
  {{command}} outbox approve 12
  {{command}} outbox discard 12 --reason "answered in person"

DOCS
  https://{{name}}hq.github.io/{{name}}/concepts/approval/
